  "verdict": "S(3) = the set of metallic ratios bracketing an active-set transition.  Empty = LP-vertex structure constant across the sweep.  {\u03c6, silver, bronze} subset = sharpened (M2) conjecture confirmed at full n=3 LP.",
  "limitations": [
    "Gram matrix uses a rank-1 outer-product + diagonal approximation.  The exact Gram requires the multiplication table of the 6 NF basis elements which is not in closed form here.  For the structural active-set transition detection, the relative ordering of t_i is the dominant factor; cross-coupling terms in G are smaller.  A more careful probe would use the pyhecke `gram_matrix()` API to get the exact G(q) \u2014 deferred.",
    "scipy.linprog in floating point: at metallic q the LP coefficients are algebraic integers in \u2124[\u03b4_n] \u2014 a symbolic solver (sympy or QSOpt-Ex) would give exact vertex coordinates.  Floating-point shadow is sufficient for active-set detection."
